{"name":"Virgin Peach","hex":"#ecbdb0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"virgin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who has never had sexual intercourse, or  an animal that has never mated.","A person who has never engaged in any sexual activity at all. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In a state of virginity; chaste, not having had sexual intercourse.","Of a physical object, untouched."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virgin"},{"term":"peach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of species Prunus persica, native to China and now widely cultivated throughout temperate regions, having pink flowers and edible fruit.","Soft juicy stone fruit of the peach tree, having yellow flesh, downy, red-tinted yellow skin, and a deeply sculptured pit or stone containing a single seed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the color peach.","Particularly pleasing or agreeable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Virginity","blocks":[{"text":"Virginity is a social construct that denotes the state of a person who has never engaged in sexual intercourse. As it is not an objective term with an operational definition, social definitions of what constitutes virginity, or the lack thereof, vary. Heterosexual individuals may or may not consider loss of virginity to occur only through penile–vaginal penetration, while people of other sexual orientations often include oral sex, anal sex, or manual sex in their definitions of virginity loss. The term \"virgin\" encompasses a range of definitions, as found in traditional, modern, and ethical concepts. Religious rituals for regaining virginity exist in many cultures. Some men and women who practice celibacy after losing their virginity consider themselves born-again virgins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-Youth_%281893%29.jpg/330px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-Youth_%281893%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginity"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree that bears edible juicy fruits with various characteristics. Most are simply called peaches, while the glossy-skinned, non-fuzzy varieties are called nectarines. Though from the same species, they are regarded commercially as different fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach"},{"title":"Peach (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Peach is a color that is named for the pale color of the interior flesh of the peach fruit. Like the color apricot, the color peach is paler than most actual peach fruits and seems to have been formulated primarily to create a pastel palette of colors for interior design."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg/500px-Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg/1280px-Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg/500px-Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A virgin and a unicorn, oil painting by an anonymous painter, ca. 1500","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChastity_(a_virgin_and_a_unicorn)._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Virgtests.jpg/330px-Virgtests.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Virgtests.jpg/330px-Virgtests.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"World Health Organization poster against virginity testing","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVirgtests.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Giorgione_045.jpg/500px-Giorgione_045.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Giorgione_045.jpg/1280px-Giorgione_045.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Giorgione_045.jpg/500px-Giorgione_045.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail of The Reading Madonna by Giorgione (c. 1500)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiorgione_045.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Virgo_inter_Virgines_IMG_1383.JPG/500px-Virgo_inter_Virgines_IMG_1383.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Virgo_inter_Virgines_IMG_1383.JPG/1280px-Virgo_inter_Virgines_IMG_1383.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f